  "worked_solution": "The transformation $y=-f(x)$ reflects the curve $y=f(x)$ in the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, notice that the point $P(-2,0)$ lies on the $x$-axis. So, under the action of the transformation, this point will be reflected to itself.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217907/assets/808bdc6ebdad390ce7bec9f2ce43dacefe8a120c6b86c48c5740e02228867b63.png)\n\nWe conclude that the point  $(-2,0)$  must lie on the graph of $y=-f(x).$",
